# Fansjoy FJ-S2 tablet calibration rule.
#
# The kernel driver reports the tablet's raw coordinates unchanged.  The
# tablet's native X axis (0..16800) and Y axis (0..10500) already match a
# landscape screen, so the verified default matrix is the identity.
#
# This rule keeps the full-tablet, no-rotation mapping explicit and prevents
# KDE/libinput from applying an unrelated rotation to this device.
#
# If you later want to rotate or mirror the pen, edit the six values below,
# then run:
#
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo udevadm trigger
#
# The six values are libinput's calibration matrix:
#   a b c
#   d e f
#
#   x' = a*x + b*y + c
#   y' = d*x + e*y + f
#
# Verified matrix (no rotation):

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2d80", ATTRS{idProduct}=="3013", ENV{ID_INPUT_TABLET}=="1", ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="1 0 0 0 1 0"
